# 3D Cinematic Website Rules

- Inspect the existing app, package versions, routing, styling, and conventions before editing.
- Follow the root `AGENTS.md` and `skills/3d-cinematic-website/SKILL.md`.
- Preserve existing functionality; avoid broad rewrites and dependency upgrades without a clear reason.
- Use Next.js App Router, TypeScript, and the project's existing styling conventions.
- Keep browser-only WebGL code in client components and dynamically load the canvas with SSR disabled.
- Keep semantic page content, SEO, navigation, and accessible controls outside the canvas.
- Use React Three Fiber and Drei for React-based 3D scenes; use GSAP/ScrollTrigger for coordinated timelines and scroll choreography; use Motion for UI transitions.
- Give every animated property one owner. Never let GSAP and `useFrame` compete for the same property.
- Load models asynchronously; include loading, error, and WebGL fallback states.
- Optimize models, textures, draw calls, shadows, post-processing, and mobile quality.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences and provide keyboard-accessible alternatives.
- Use only original or properly licensed assets. Verify commercial-use and modification rights.
- Do not copy Transformers characters, names, logos, or recognizable designs without written authorization.
- Build in milestones. First complete and test the responsive 3D hero before expanding to other sections.
- Run the project's actual lint, type-check, and build scripts after meaningful changes.
- Never claim tests, performance, licenses, or deployment succeeded unless verified.
